---
import Banner from '../components/astro/content/Banner.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/astro/content/Header.astro';
import Projects from '../components/astro/Projects.astro';
import Footer from '../components/astro/content/Footer.astro';
import CookieBanner from '../components/react/CookieBanner.jsx';
import GitHub from '../components/icons/GitHub';
import LinkedIn from '../components/icons/LinkedIn';
import Link from '../components/astro/Link.astro';
import { getLangFromUrl, useTranslations } from '../i18n/utils';

const t = useTranslations(getLangFromUrl(Astro.url));
---

<Layout>
    <Header />
    <Banner />
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto my-12 md:my-24 px-4">
        <h2
            id="about-me"
            class="text-5xl mb-6 font-title font-black tracking-wide"
        >
            About Me
        </h2>

        <p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
            Hi, I’m Camila and this is my story. I studied biochemistry in Chile
            and wrote my thesis in the Department of Cell Biology, researching
            <a
                href="https://www.mdpi.com/2673-7140/4/1/1"
                target="_blank"
                class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline"
            >
                how heavy alcohol consumption affects adolescence.
            </a> After finishing university, I chased one of my big dreams: living
            abroad. I first went to Ireland to improve my English, then moved to
            Germany, where I enrolled in a master’s program in biochemistry at the
            University of Cologne. A difficult experience during an internship triggered
            an anxiety crisis that made me rethink my priorities. Together with my
            husband, we decided to move to France, a country that offered new opportunities,
            a friendlier language, and plenty of sunshine and beaches.
        </p>

        <p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
            In France I faced the typical challenges of a new life: cultural
            adaptation, job hunting, and the language barrier. After several
            months without finding a position in my highly specialized field, I
            had two options: specialize in another area to stay in science, or
            start something completely new. And here I am—you can guess which
            path I chose.
        </p>

        <p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
            It’s been a lot of fun, but also quite challenging for me. I’ve
            learned so much, rewiring my brain to grasp new concepts and think
            differently. In science and programming, there’s lots of knowledge
            we can transfer, yet there’s also plenty of new material to
            integrate. Truly the best of both worlds.
        </p>

        <!-- <p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
            While studying to become a web developer, my baby arrived.
            Motherhood brought sleepless nights and a mountain of challenges,
            but also an unexpected strength: I managed to finish my training
            despite everything. Becoming parents changes everything, and we
            realized we needed a “village” around us to raise our child. That’s
            why we decided to move to Belgium. Being close to his family gives
            us the support and community we want for raising our kid, and it
            fills us with energy to keep moving forward.
        </p> -->

        <h3 class="text-3xl mb-6 font-title font-black tracking-wide">
            <span class="inline-block rotate-180 mr-1">?</span>Why Web
            Development?
        </h3>

        <p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
            A few years ago I discovered a game for learning programming:
            <a
                href="https://codecombat.com/user/cararcel"
                target="_blank"
                class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">CodeCombat</a
            >. I started playing for fun and learned a lot. Then I decided to
            take some courses to dive deeper. The first ones were on
            <a
                href="https://laracasts.com/"
                target="_blank"
                class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">Laracasts</a
            >. I watched videos on HTML, CSS, and PHP. Jeffrey Way explains
            things very well; everything looks simple, and I was behind the
            screen trying to figure out why it didn’t work for me (spoiler
            alert: sometimes it was just a typo).
        </p>

        <p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
            Later I discovered
            <a
                href="https://grafikart.fr"
                target="_blank"
                class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">Grafikart</a
            >, which was great for me because I could practice my French (at
            least understand it) while continuing to learn. I revisited HTML and
            CSS and kept going with JavaScript.
        </p>

        <p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
            Deciding to go back to school (officially) was tough, but I wanted
            to formalize the knowledge I already had and keep learning more
            about web development. So I enrolled in a career‑change program at
            <a
                href="https://openclassrooms.com/fr/paths/899-developpeur-web"
                target="_blank"
                class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">OpenClassrooms</a
            >. Now I can say I am
            <a
                href="/assets/oc-certificat.pdf"
                title="my OpenClassrooms certificate"
                target="_blank"
                class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline"
            >
                officially a web developer.</a
            > ¡Hoorray!
        </p>

        <p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
            After finishing my training I devoted myself to motherhood and
            personal projects that keep me up‑to‑date (or at least prevent my
            skills from rusting). Currently I’m learning more about React
            through the
            <a
                href="https://www.epicreact.dev/"
                target="_blank"
                class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">Epic React</a
            >
            course.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 mt-8 md:items-center">
            <span class="text-xl font-black">Find me on:</span>
            <div class="flex gap-4">
                <Link
                    title={t('My GitHub repository')}
                    className="bg-white px-3 py-2"
                    target="_blank"
                    href="https://github.com/cararcel"
                >
                    <GitHub className="size-6" />GitHub
                </Link>

                <Link
                    title={t('My LinkedIn profile')}
                    className="bg-blue-600 text-white px-3 py-2"
                    target="_blank"
                    href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/arce-camila/"
                >
                    <LinkedIn className="size-6 fill-current" />LinkedIn
                </Link>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <Projects />
    <Footer />
    <CookieBanner client:load trans={t('cookie')} />
</Layout>
